{%- comment -%}
  The "Notify Me" button, in one place.

  The button was built twice - once in card-product, once in main-product - and both copies
  carried the same three lines of plumbing: capture the output of lena-notify-target, strip
  it, split it on the pipe, and pass the two halves to window.lenaNotify in the right order.
  Getting that order wrong swaps the label and the handle, which files the signup under the
  wrong category without failing or showing anything odd on screen. That is exactly the kind
  of rule that should not be written twice.

  USAGE

    {%- render 'lena-notify-button', product: card_product, style: 'card' -%}
    {%- render 'lena-notify-button', product: product, style: 'pdp' -%}

    product  the sold-out product. Required.
    style    'card' -> "Notify Me",               class lena-notify-btn
             'pdp'  -> "Notify me of similar items", class lena-pdp-notify-btn
             Anything else falls back to 'card'.

  The button renders nothing for a product that is still available, so a call site cannot
  produce a Notify Me button next to an Add to cart button by forgetting a guard. Call sites
  that need to wrap other sold-out content keep their own `unless` as well; the two agree.

  The category comes from lena-notify-target, never from product.type - the two disagree for
  five of the seven live categories.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product.available == false -%}
  {%- liquid
    case style
      when 'pdp'
        assign nb_class = 'lena-pdp-notify-btn'
        assign nb_label = 'Notify me of similar items'
      else
        assign nb_class = 'lena-notify-btn'
        assign nb_label = 'Notify Me'
    endcase
  -%}
  {%- capture nb_target -%}{%- render 'lena-notify-target', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign nb_parts = nb_target | strip | split: '|' -%}
  <button class="{{ nb_class }}" type="button"
    onclick="window.lenaNotify('{{ nb_parts[1] | escape }}','{{ nb_parts[0] | escape }}')">
    <span class="dm sm"></span> {{ nb_label }}
  </button>
{%- endif -%}
